      "ihh:review": {
        "ihh:state": "pending"
      },
      "ihh:notes": "Conflicting: KU Spencer finding aid (NAI-S-0017) says orphaned in 1873; Dictionary of Canadian Biography (NAI-S-0018) says 'After the deaths of their parents in 1870'; Kansas Historical Society (NAI-S-0019) says 'Orphaned at the age of nine' (born 1861). A person decides; not used in tour copy.\nRuling 2026-10-16 (owner rule: a primary record decides; CONFLICTS.md): orphaned 1873 is contradicted: the father, John Naismith, carpenter and joiner, formerly of Almonte, 'died on or about the Eighteenth day of October, A.D. 1870' (Almonte Gazette, 22 Sept 1871, p. 3, notice to creditors; Mississippi Valley Textile Museum). No primary record of the mother's death was found, so the site gives no year for the orphaning."
    },
