      "ihh:notes": "Conflicting day: Kansas Historical Society (NAI-S-0019) and Dictionary of Canadian Biography (NAI-S-0018, 'm. first 20 June 1894 Maude Evelyn Sherman') say June 20, 1894; KU Spencer finding aid (NAI-S-0017) says 'On June 2, 1894'. The year 1894 is supported by all three. A person decides.\nRuling 2026-10-16 (owner rule: a primary record decides; CONFLICTS.md): 20 June 1894 decided by the Springfield Weekly Republican, Friday 22 June 1894, p. 12 (LoC Chronicling America): 'the wedding Wednesday night of ... James Naismith, to Miss Maude E. Sherman ... in Hope church'; 20 June 1894 was that Wednesday (2 June was a Saturday). Released from conflicting; the KU 'June 2' is not used."
